{"parentUuid":"e6d87201-aed9-4ddf-a6f7-ae2d92ff304d","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YKcTAnY8psuBiJ9LV8sUge","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT ResponseStats num_conflicts num_branches fields\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: Google.OrTools.Sat.CpSolverResponse Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/dotnet/classGoogle_1_1OrTools_1_1Sat_1_1CpSolverResponse.html\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT claims to find optimal solution to a MILP\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/4fcAuWiIUFA\"},{\"title\":\"ortools cp_solver conflicting constraints · Issue #1398 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1398\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: ortools.sat.python.cp_model.CpSolver Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/python/classortools_1_1sat_1_1python_1_1cp__model_1_1CpSolver.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"trying to solve huge mode on CP-Sat\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/VjiSYjFFB_4\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about the `ResponseStats` fields in OR-Tools CP-SAT solver:\n\nThe `num_branches` and `num_conflicts` fields are part of the CpSolverResponse class. These fields represent the number of search branches explored by the solver and the number of conflicts encountered since the creation of the solver, respectively.\n\nIn the context of the solver's output, these statistics are typically included in the response summary. For example, in solver logs you can see output like: \"booleans: 11983731 conflicts: 0 branches: 10218\" which displays these key metrics along with other statistics such as propagations, restarts, and LP iterations.\n\nThe statistics about the solve correspond to the statistics of the first subsolver in multithread mode, which is usually the one with the user defined parameters or the default-search if none are specified.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3b35369f-bcf7-445a-b5a9-a2a448247182","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:00.650Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"e6d87201-aed9-4ddf-a6f7-ae2d92ff304d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"5bafe5c2-80d3-4549-825b-d28dbb66673f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01C3vTLHBNw83TxiN3xVYJ2k","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT log_search_progress log format fields explanation 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"visibility to CP-SAT solver progress metric in Java\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/CEdRanlYa0o\"},{\"title\":\"cpsat-logutils · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/cpsat-logutils/\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"enable the log of CP-SAT solver · google/or-tools · Discussion #3873\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3873\"},{\"title\":\"Coding Patterns - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/06_coding_patterns.html\"},{\"title\":\"Debugging the model\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/x84toCnIWnU/m/nyF4cJ-XAwAJ\"},{\"title\":\"sat_proto_solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/linear_solver/sat_proto_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Log search progress with structured data\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/p8hdRwrYybE\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's an explanation of the OR-Tools CP-SAT `log_search_progress` log format fields:\n\n## Log Structure Overview\n\nThe structure of the log entries is standardized as follows: EVENT NAME | TIME | BEST SOLUTION | RANGE OF THE SEARCH | COMMENT.\n\n## Key Fields Explained\n\n**Event Types:**\n- An event marked #2 indicates the discovery of the second solution\n- A notation like best:16 confirms that the solver has found a solution with a value of 16. An event with #Bound denotes an enhancement in the bound, as seen by a reduction in the RANGE OF THE SEARCH.\n\n**Response Summary Fields:**\n\nThe status of the search can be FEASIBLE, OPTIMAL, INFEASIBLE, UNKNOWN, or MODEL_INVALID.\n\nThe objective field shows the value of the objective function for the best solution found. The best_bound field shows the proven bound on the objective function, i.e., the best possible value.\n\nFields include integers, booleans, conflicts, branches, propagations, integer_propagations, restarts, lp_iterations, and walltime (the time in seconds since solver creation).\n\nThe gap_integral field represents the integral of the gap over time. A lower value will indicate that the solver is converging faster.\n\nThe solution_fingerprint field is useful to check if two runs result in the same solution.\n\n## Enabling Logging\n\nThe log_search_progress parameter is crucial at the beginning. It enables logging of the search progress, providing insights into how CP-SAT solves your problem.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c536554c-bf1f-4445-9088-df7dfee0cd94","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:01.582Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5bafe5c2-80d3-4549-825b-d28dbb66673f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6577123e-7433-4e5d-96ac-2e9f6499246a","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015DdvQs6bgPuiX2mHUHA4z8","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT solver log_callback log parsing conflicts learned clauses\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-logutils: Utils for parsing the logs of OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-logutils\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"cpsat-logutils · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/cpsat-logutils/\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: com.google.ortools.sat.CpSolver Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/java/classcom_1_1google_1_1ortools_1_1sat_1_1CpSolver.html\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Constraint Programming Solver | google/or-tools | DeepWiki\",\"url\":\"https://deepwiki.com/google/or-tools/4.1-cp-sat-constraint-programming-solver\"},{\"title\":\"Enhancing Hybrid CP-SAT Search for Disjunctive Scheduling\",\"url\":\"https://hal.science/hal-04174800/document\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about CP-SAT solver log parsing, the log_callback, conflicts, and learned clauses:\n\n## Log Callback and Parsing\n\nIn Python, you can capture logs via solver.log_callback = my_fn to avoid duplicates. The cpsat-logutils library extracts key information from CP-SAT logs (solutions, bounds, presolve stats, subsolver activity, search progress, conflicts, etc.) and exposes them in structured Python objects you can analyze or visualize.\n\n## Conflicts and Learned Clauses\n\nThe key technique that makes SAT solving efficient is conflict-driven clause learning (CDCL). When the solver hits a dead end (a conflict where no valid assignment exists), it analyzes why the conflict occurred and learns a new clause preventing similar conflicts.\n\nThe analysis produces a learned clause like \"NOT x OR NOT y\" meaning \"x and y cannot both be true.\" This clause is added to the problem permanently (for the duration of the solve). Over the course of solving, the solver might learn thousands or millions of clauses.\n\n## Restarts and Learned Clauses\n\nRestarts rebuild the search tree from scratch, but keep learned clauses. This allows to recover from bad decisions, and lead to smaller search trees by learning from the mistakes of the past.\n\nIf you're interested in parsing CP-SAT logs programmatically, the cpsat-logutils library and CP-SAT Log Analyzer tool are designed specifically for this purpose and can help analyze conflicts and clause learning data from solver output.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"060b2a82-c267-4f16-9cd9-ca75739668f8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:02.010Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6577123e-7433-4e5d-96ac-2e9f6499246a","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4ebfa3b0-3af0-48ea-8ca1-3d6aff5413f2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01M6RMbQrCsS5T77jQCUxkZ4","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT LRAT proof checker 2025 unsat certificate\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Fast and Verified UNSAT Certificate Checking | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-63498-7_26\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - lammich/lrat_isa: Fast and formally verified UNSAT certificate checker\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/lammich/lrat_isa\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Verified (UN)SAT Certificate Checking | Journal of Automated Reasoning | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10817-019-09525-z\"},{\"title\":\"Fast and Verified UNSAT Certificate Checking - University of Twente Research Information\",\"url\":\"https://research.utwente.nl/en/publications/fast-andverified-unsat-certificate-checking/\"},{\"title\":\"Fast and Verified UNSAT Certificate Checking\",\"url\":\"https://www21.in.tum.de/~lammich/isabelle_llvm_par/IJCAR2024.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Fast and Verified UNSAT Certificate Checking | Automated Reasoning\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1007/978-3-031-63498-7_26\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Fast and Verified UNSAT Certificate Checking\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/381859387_Fast_and_Verified_UNSAT_Certificate_Checking\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Efficient Verified (UN)SAT Certificate Checking\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/333612067_Efficient_Verified_UNSAT_Certificate_Checking\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Certified RAT Verification⋆ - UT Computer Science\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.utexas.edu/~marijn/publications/lrat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Verified (UN)SAT Certificate Checking\",\"url\":\"https://d-nb.info/1195523297/34\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found comprehensive information about LRAT proof checkers and UNSAT certificates:\n\n## Overview\n\nA formally verified checker for unsatisfiability certificates in the LRAT format can be run in parallel with the SAT solver, processing the certificate while it is being produced.\n\n## Key Implementation Details\n\nlrat_isa is a checker for unsatisfiability certificates in the LRUP format, formally verified in Isabelle/HOL. The checker accepts the LRUP fragment of the LRAT format, which makes it suitable for checking certificates from many top-performing SAT solvers.\n\n## Verification Approach\n\nThe verification is done with respect to a grammar of the DIMACS format and a semantics of CNF formulas, down to the LLVM code of the checker, using the Isabelle-LLVM stepwise refinement approach.\n\n## Performance Characteristics\n\nIt is implemented time and memory efficiently, and can be run in parallel to the SAT solver at low overhead. For CaDiCaL, this is only 10% slower than running just the solver, and 2% slower than writing the certificate to a file without checking it.\n\nThe search results primarily focus on research from 2019-2024, with a 2024 IJCAR conference paper being the most recent publication on this topic.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"dc2d1251-c96e-4a36-91fa-a1054ead3d0b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:03.088Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4ebfa3b0-3af0-48ea-8ca1-3d6aff5413f2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
