{"parentUuid":"7635aa42-c06c-4c5f-bcf1-620fdc769acc","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01CWmM49i1PtxNjneEYqk4En","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LqX3a1TeVGfYorQRTNjPaJ","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/dotnet/classGoogle_1_1OrTools_1_1Sat_1_1CpSolverResponse.html","prompt":"List all fields in CpSolverResponse, especially statistics fields: num_conflicts, num_branches, num_booleans, num_binary_propagations, num_integer_propagations, num_restarts, num_lp_iterations, sufficient_assumptions_for_infeasibility, solution, solution_info, etc. Anything that helps mining conflicts."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5319,"cache_read_input_tokens":21262,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5319,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaorhBV3gKquYEvwjeJUo","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"4a5937b6-76fb-453d-ac7a-fa9995206448","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:13.654Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4a5937b6-76fb-453d-ac7a-fa9995206448","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01CWmM49i1PtxNjneEYqk4En","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XUFJJ9moSwGu7iQP3aa6WL","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"CP-SAT sufficient_assumptions_for_infeasibility unsat core extraction"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5319,"cache_read_input_tokens":21262,"output_tokens":740,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5319},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":740,"cache_read_input_tokens":21262,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5319,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5319,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaorhBV3gKquYEvwjeJUo","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"743c3de1-ccce-457b-a8a3-ca2d615f1178","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:13.926Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"310c739f-d60b-4538-a0cb-f1b3684ea36f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UykNN5VvKu3tpzPuTwM3BC","type":"tool_result","content":"# cpsat-logutils: Extraction Capabilities & APIs\n\n## Information Extracted\n\nBased on the documentation, cpsat-logutils extracts:\n\n- **Solver metadata**: version, worker count, parameters\n- **Model statistics**: variable/constraint counts (initial and presolved)\n- **Presolve outcomes**: whether problem solved during presolve\n- **Search progress**: events, timing, bounds, objective values\n- **Task timing**: subsolver activity breakdowns\n- **Search statistics**: progress metrics\n- **Final response**: status and objective value\n\nThe library focuses on \"solutions, bounds, presolve stats, subsolver activity, search progress\" from CP-SAT logs.\n\n## Parser Classes\n\nThe documentation explicitly names these block types:\n- `SolverBlock`\n- `InitialModelBlock`\n- `PresolvedModelBlock`\n- `PresolveSummaryBlock`\n- `SearchProgressBlock`\n- `TaskTimingBlock`\n- `SearchStatsBlock`\n- `ObjectiveBoundsBlock`\n- `ResponseBlock`\n\n## Notable Limitations\n\n**Not documented**: The webpage does not explicitly detail extractable fields for conflicts, learned clauses, partial assignments, or conflict-driven search information. These topics aren't mentioned in the provided content, suggesting either they're not extracted or require examining the source code's `blocks/` directory beyond what's shown here.\n\n## API Pattern\n\nThe library uses a fluent parser interface:\n```python\nparser = LogParser(raw_log)\nparser.get_block_of_type_or_none(BlockClass)\n```\nBlocks expose methods returning structured data (dicts, pandas DataFrames, or event lists)."}]},"uuid":"e3b327ae-6398-41ec-beeb-b1b0114f2e34","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:15.420Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"310c739f-d60b-4538-a0cb-f1b3684ea36f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7635aa42-c06c-4c5f-bcf1-620fdc769acc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011Veo4aKh3dQmyzvgVfP4WT","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Log Structure Overview\n\nBased on the CP-SAT Primer content, here are the main log sections and fields:\n\n## Key Log Sections\n\n**Initialization**\n- CP-SAT version, parameters, worker count\n\n**Initial Model Description**\n- Variable counts (booleans, integers)\n- Variable domains\n- Constraint types with counts (#kBoolOr, #kLinear1, #kLinear2, etc.)\n\n**Presolve Log**\n- Individual rule applications and their effects\n- Timing for presolve operations\n- Affine relations detected\n- Variable elimination statistics\n\n**Presolved Model**\n- Post-presolve variable and constraint summary\n- Modified constraint types and counts\n\n**Preloading Model**\n- Initial bound information\n- Symmetry detection results\n\n**Search Phase**\n- Event entries showing: time, best solution, search range, contributing subsolver\n- Event types: #N (solutions), #Bound (improvements), #Model (modifications)\n\n**Subsolver Details**\n- Task timing per subsolver\n- Clause sharing statistics\n- Cutting plane information\n\n## CpSolverResponse Summary Fields\n\nThe primer explicitly lists these response fields:\n- status (FEASIBLE, OPTIMAL, INFEASIBLE, UNKNOWN, MODEL_INVALID)\n- objective value\n- best_bound\n- integers, booleans counts\n- \"conflicts: 0\"\n- \"branches: 370\"\n- \"propagations: 13193\"\n- \"integer_propagations: 6897\"\n- restarts\n- lp_iterations\n- walltime, usertime, deterministic_time\n- gap_integral\n- solution_fingerprint\n\n**Note:** The provided content doesn't detail UNSAT cores or extensive conflict logging beyond the conflict count field shown."}]},"uuid":"6d45dcfb-3912-45fa-97d4-d117e8a62b33","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:16.249Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7635aa42-c06c-4c5f-bcf1-620fdc769acc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"4a5937b6-76fb-453d-ac7a-fa9995206448","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LqX3a1TeVGfYorQRTNjPaJ","type":"tool_result","content":"# CpSolverResponse Fields Overview\n\nThe `CpSolverResponse` class contains numerous fields for analyzing solver behavior and extracting conflict information:\n\n## Core Solution Fields\n- **Status**: The solve completion status\n- **Solution**: \"A feasible solution to the given problem\" with variable values\n- **ObjectiveValue**: The objective value of the returned solution\n- **BestObjectiveBound**: Proven bound on the objective\n\n## Statistics Fields\n- **NumConflicts**: Count of conflicts encountered during solving\n- **NumBranches**: Number of branch decisions made\n- **NumBooleans**: Boolean variable count\n- **NumIntegers**: Integer variable count\n- **NumFixedBooleans**: Fixed boolean variable count\n- **NumBinaryPropagations**: Binary constraint propagation count\n- **NumIntegerPropagations**: Integer constraint propagation count\n- **NumRestarts**: Search restart count\n- **NumLpIterations**: Linear programming iteration count\n\n## Conflict Analysis Fields\n- **SufficientAssumptionsForInfeasibility**: \"A subset of the model assumptions field\" provided when status is INFEASIBLE, representing assumptions needed for infeasibility\n- **TightenedVariables**: Reduced variable domains derived during solving\n\n## Additional Diagnostic Fields\n- **SolutionInfo**: \"Additional information about how the solution was found\" and model/parameter errors\n- **SolveLog**: Solver output log (when enabled)\n- **AdditionalSolutions**: Alternative solutions from the internal solution pool\n- **WallTime**, **UserTime**, **DeterministicTime**: Timing metrics\n- **GapIntegral**: Objective gap integral over time\n\nThese fields enable comprehensive analysis of solver performance and conflict extraction."}]},"uuid":"4025086d-3ec5-442c-a10d-122c56a0918d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:20.039Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"4a5937b6-76fb-453d-ac7a-fa9995206448","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"743c3de1-ccce-457b-a8a3-ca2d615f1178","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XUFJJ9moSwGu7iQP3aa6WL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT sufficient_assumptions_for_infeasibility unsat core extraction\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Solving with assumptions — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/unsat_core_extraction.html\"},{\"title\":\"UnSAT core extraction with assumptions — CPMpy 0.9.23 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/linearize-power/unsat_core_extraction.html\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"UnSAT core extraction with assumptions — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/complex_sudoku_examples/unsat_core_extraction.html\"},{\"title\":\"UnSAT core extraction with assumption variables — CPMpy 0.9.21 ...\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/unsat_core_extraction.html\"},{\"title\":\"python cp-sat unsat assumption bug, is sat · Issue #2649 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/2649\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools: ortools/sat/docs/troubleshooting.md | Fossies\",\"url\":\"https://fossies.org/linux/or-tools/ortools/sat/docs/troubleshooting.md\"},{\"title\":\"Unsat core and clause assumptions\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/minisat/c/NtGX_CZ9MKA\"},{\"title\":\"Optimization with Python: Infeasibility Explanation for Integer Programming with Google OR Tools | by Zia | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@ZiaH919/optimization-with-python-infeasibility-explanation-for-integer-programming-with-or-tools-7372b64322d\"},{\"title\":\"Journal of Artiﬁcial Intelligence Research 40 (2011) 701-728\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1401.3878\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about CP-SAT's `sufficient_assumptions_for_infeasibility` and unsat core extraction:\n\n## CP-SAT Unsat Core Extraction\n\nCP-SAT implements a mechanism of assumptions to find the root cause of an infeasible problem. To use it, one must add enforcement literals to constraints and add these literals to the set of assumptions.\n\n## The sufficient_assumptions_for_infeasibility Method\n\nCP-SAT offers the capability to extract unsatisfiable cores from infeasible models. By enabling constraints conditionally using only_enforce_if(b) and adding b as an assumption, one can isolate sources of infeasibility. If the model proves infeasible, CP-SAT can return a minimal subset of the assumptions, and thus the corresponding constraints, that lead to the conflict.\n\nThe method `sufficient_assumptions_for_infeasibility()` (or `sufficient_assumptions_for_infeasibility` in Python) returns the indices of these conflicting assumptions when the model is infeasible.\n\n## Important Limitation\n\nNote that this set is minimized but not guaranteed to be minimal.\n\n## Practical Use Case\n\nThe method is called after solving: `for var_index in solver.sufficient_assumptions_for_infeasibility(): print(f\"{var_index}: '{model.proto.variables[var_index].name}'\")` to display which constraints are involved in the infeasibility.\n\nThis feature enables debugging of infeasible constraint programming models by identifying which constraints conflict with each other.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"8bb23b6b-6907-4e25-8085-faf890c82de9","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:20.847Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"743c3de1-ccce-457b-a8a3-ca2d615f1178","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
