{"parentUuid":"cdf5e644-1a7c-4dad-b748-15faf22615fe","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PGjQRzyY3ZzsyW4fuhxMVG","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools github issue extract learned clauses CP-SAT Laurent Perron\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Laurent Perron (lperron@google.com)\",\"url\":\"https://egon.cheme.cmu.edu/ewo/docs/CP-SAT%20and%20OR-Tools.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT get's stuck when trying to maximize sum of boolean variables that are all added as assumptions · google/or-tools · Discussion #3630\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3630\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT, UNKNOWN status with complete solution hint · Issue #3750 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3750\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT: Best way to find infeasible constraints · Issue #973 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/973\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT produces nondeterministic results · Issue #3590 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3590\"},{\"title\":\"CP-Sat: Python 3.7.2, ortools 7.0 wrong optimization result · Issue #1162 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/1162\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/tree/stable/ortools/sat\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found several relevant resources about OR-Tools, CP-SAT, and Laurent Perron:\n\n1. **OR-Tools Documentation**: Inferred clauses are checked with an LRAT checker as they are learned, in presolve and in each worker, which relates to clause learning in CP-SAT.\n\n2. **Laurent Perron's Work**: Clause Learning is critical as it offsets the cost of running the simplex, according to a presentation by Laurent Perron on CP-SAT and OR-Tools.\n\n3. **CP-SAT Architecture**: The directory contains a next-gen Constraint Programming solver with clause learning, built on top of an efficient SAT/max-SAT solver.\n\nThe search results show that while there are references to clause learning and extraction mechanisms in OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver (with Laurent Perron being a key contributor), the specific GitHub issue about extracting learned clauses isn't directly appearing in these results. The functionality appears to relate to LRAT proof checking and clause learning mechanisms, but a more specific GitHub issue link would require searching for additional details.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"4ef06646-88b5-4bbc-bb3f-3faf5c9c9b84","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:28.818Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cdf5e644-1a7c-4dad-b748-15faf22615fe","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d082c396-c19c-4c62-a83c-3c248e0b81ed","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AKEXodGFUoK6bVzjW269cT","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT solution_callback intermediate partial assignment hooks\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"Find many CP-SAT solutions, multi-threaded, under time constraint\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/GNgvcMpEwmE\"},{\"title\":\"Google AI’s OR-Tools CP-SAT Solver unofficial tutorial Bobak Pezeshki\",\"url\":\"https://ics.uci.edu/~dechter/courses/ics-275/fall-2020/slides/OR-Tools_CP-SAT_Solver_Tutorial.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"Obtaining Intermediate Solutions in OR-Tools CP-SAT [Fixed]\",\"url\":\"https://www.technetexperts.com/ortools-intermediate-solutions-callback/\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: ortools.sat.python.cp_model.CpSolverSolutionCallback Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/python/classortools_1_1sat_1_1python_1_1cp__model_1_1CpSolverSolutionCallback.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/examples/python/flexible_job_shop_sat.py at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/examples/python/flexible_job_shop_sat.py\"},{\"title\":\"Best way to generate multiple optimal/close-to-optimal solutions with CP-SAT\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/4DeoO5f7YXQ\"}]\n\nI found relevant information about OR-Tools CP-SAT solution callbacks and intermediate solutions. Here's a summary of the search results:\n\n## CP-SAT Solution Callback\n\nThe `CpSolverSolutionCallback` class implements a callback that will be called at each new solution found during search, and the method `on_solution_callback()` must be implemented. The current solution can be queried using the `boolean_value()` and `value()` methods.\n\n## Intermediate Solutions\n\nThe solution printer is a callback that you pass to the solver, which displays each solution as it is found. The CP-SAT solver provides a callback interface designed to monitor the search process for tracking progress, logging metrics, or storing suboptimal but feasible results.\n\nWhen solving an optimization problem with an objective function, the CP-SAT solver internally adds a dynamic constraint, and every time a solution is found, the solver ensures that any subsequent solution must strictly improve the objective value, so the default `on_solution_callback()` method is only triggered when a better solution is discovered.\n\n## Partial Assignments & Hints\n\nRegarding partial assignments, the search results mention completing partial hints into full variable assignments, as CP-SAT only benefits from complete hints (all variables hinted).\n\nThe search results don't contain specific information about \"intermediate partial assignment hooks\" as a specific feature. If you need more detailed information about that particular aspect, please let me know and I can search for additional resources.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"95e4af23-ebab-49ce-ad03-8211396f822a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:31.275Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d082c396-c19c-4c62-a83c-3c248e0b81ed","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8c707a4e-6b5e-4f8f-94a5-21ea4549b110","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H263R4CBDb76vLBqvErBjS","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"PySAT MUS extraction QuickXplain DEL minimal unsat subset 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Solving with assumptions — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/unsat_core_extraction.html\"},{\"title\":\"A deletion-based MUS extractor (pysat.examples.musx) — PySAT 1.8.dev26 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/docs/html/api/examples/musx.html\"},{\"title\":\"UnSAT core extraction with assumption variables — CPMpy 0.9.21 ...\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/unsat_core_extraction.html\"},{\"title\":\"UnSAT core extraction with assumptions — CPMpy 0.9.23 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/linearize-power/unsat_core_extraction.html\"},{\"title\":\"UnSAT core extraction with assumptions — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/complex_sudoku_examples/unsat_core_extraction.html\"},{\"title\":\"Explanation tools (cpmpy.tools.explain) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/simpl_bool_fix/api/tools/explain.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - pysathq/pysat: A toolkit for SAT-based prototyping in Python · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pysathq/pysat\"},{\"title\":\"pysat/examples/musx.py at master · pysathq/pysat\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pysathq/pysat/blob/master/examples/musx.py\"},{\"title\":\"PySAT: A Python Toolkit for Prototyping with SAT Oracles ⋆\",\"url\":\"https://alexeyignatiev.github.io/assets/pdf/imms-sat18-preprint.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"OptUx optimal MUS enumerator (pysat.examples.optux) — PySAT 1.9.dev1 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/docs/html/api/examples/optux.html\"}]\n\nI've found several relevant results about PySAT MUS (Minimal Unsatisfiable Subset) extraction. Here's what the search revealed:\n\n## PySAT MUS Extraction\n\nPySAT implements a deletion-based algorithm for extracting a minimal unsatisfiable subset (MUS) of a given unsatisfiable CNF formula.\n\n### Deletion-Based Algorithm\n\nThe deletion-based MUS extraction method works by using an over-approximation of an MUS (an unsatisfiable core from a SAT oracle), then removes a clause from the core at each iteration and checks whether the remaining clauses of the approximation are unsatisfiable together with the hard clauses.\n\n### QuickXplain Implementation\n\nQuickXplain is an algorithm that finds a preferred minimal unsatisfiable subset of constraints based on their ordering, imposing a total order on the constraints using the ordering of soft constraints, with an assumption-based implementation for solvers that support assumptions.\n\n### PySAT Capabilities\n\nPySAT is helpful for implementing MUS/MCS extractors or enumerators. Additionally, OptUx is an implementation of a smallest size minimal unsatisfiable subset (SMUS) extractor and enumerator based on implicit hitting set enumeration, supporting both plain CNF formulas and weighted WCNF formulas to compute and enumerate optimal MUSes.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"2a0fd7fc-5f46-4e31-9cc9-26e618fde94c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:31.444Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8c707a4e-6b5e-4f8f-94a5-21ea4549b110","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d9585863-c694-4396-bee4-53e37cea7b6e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"fa4d4bc6-e2b2-445f-8cd0-cc97f0106215","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CZKJMqF9CCavRzW5Bbist8","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT export DRAT proof unsat certificate or-tools github\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"UNSAT Certificates\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2022/certificates.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - marijnheule/drat-trim: The DRAT-trim proof checker\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/marijnheule/drat-trim\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/tree/stable/ortools/sat\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2023/certificates.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_solver.h at master · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/master/ortools/sat/sat_solver.h\"},{\"title\":\"GRAT: a formally veriﬁed (UN)SAT proof checker Proof Checker Proposal\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2023/downloads/proposals/grat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Competition 2020\",\"url\":\"https://satcompetition.github.io/2020/certificates.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about CP-SAT and DRAT proof export in OR-Tools:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**OR-Tools Support for DRAT Proofs:**\n\nOR-Tools includes `drat_writer.h` which writes UNSAT proofs in the DRAT format, allowing verification of UNSAT proofs with the third-party program DRAT-trim.\n\n**Configuration Options:**\n\nIn the `sat_parameters.proto` file, there are parameters `check_drat_proof` and `output_lrat_proof` for handling DRAT proofs. As of November 2025, DRAT proof checking only works for pure SAT problems with single workers, no presolve, and linearization level ≤ 1.\n\nIf `output_drat_proof` is true, a DRAT proof is output to a file for SAT problems meeting specific constraints.\n\n**DRAT Format Overview:**\n\nThe DRAT proof format is backwards compatible with both the DRUP and RUP formats, and DRAT-trim can be used to validate that a proof is a certificate of unsatisfiability of a formula.\n\nYou can find the relevant OR-Tools code in the GitHub repository at `google/or-tools` in the `ortools/sat` directory, where the DRAT writer and solver parameters are implemented.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c75c4110-a9d0-4dbe-a161-cf0f5ce3fa2b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:32.239Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d9585863-c694-4396-bee4-53e37cea7b6e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
