{"parentUuid":"7578d1c9-8da7-4096-afb9-fda8d4a7c8e0","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_014vgoCxiW1FoShQahDZbeXF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TTyM53x8QJKo99geL2ucMH","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"or-tools\" \"share_binary_clauses\" \"share_glue_clauses\" worker clause sharing"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5301,"cache_read_input_tokens":30565,"output_tokens":690,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5301},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":690,"cache_read_input_tokens":30565,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5301,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5301,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaorjLJvVNNtDYKthMNLW","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"243c76bc-3854-4c27-a2ce-fb731539d7dc","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:42.469Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c6b3afbf-18af-456d-a398-0be4f4737fdf","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"58edd382-d924-48ac-8751-7dee8400aa54","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CuqYNXGEzVu7icZQ5VBrhM","type":"tool_result","content":"# SAT Parameters Reference\n\nBased on the file content, here are the requested parameters:\n\n## DRAT Proof Parameters\n- **check_drat_proof** (bool, default=false): \"If true, and if the problem is UNSAT, a DRAT proof of this UNSAT property is checked after the solver has finished.\"\n- **output_drat_proof** (bool, default=false): \"If true, a DRAT proof that all the clauses inferred by the solver are valid is output to a file.\"\n- **max_drat_time_in_seconds** (double, default=inf): Maximum time allowed to verify the DRAT proof.\n\n## LRAT Proof Parameters\n- **check_lrat_proof** (bool, default=false): \"If true, inferred clauses are checked with an LRAT checker as they are learned, in presolve and in each worker.\"\n- **output_lrat_proof** (bool, default=false): \"If true, an LRAT proof that all the clauses inferred by the solver are valid is output to several files.\"\n- **check_merged_lrat_proof** (bool, default=false): Validates merged proof file correctness for UNSAT problems.\n- **debug_crash_if_lrat_check_fails** (bool, default=false): Crash if LRAT UNSAT proof validation fails.\n\n## Clause Sharing Parameters\n- **share_binary_clauses** (bool, default=true): \"Allows sharing of new learned binary clause between workers.\"\n- **share_glue_clauses** (bool, default=true): \"Allows sharing of short glue clauses between workers.\"\n- **share_glue_clauses_dtime** (double, default=1.0): Time interval between exporting shared glue clauses.\n- **minimize_shared_clauses** (bool, default=true): Minimize and detect subsumption of shared clauses after import.\n\n## Logging Parameters\n- **log_search_progress** (bool, default=false): \"Whether the solver should log the search progress.\"\n- **log_subsolver_statistics** (bool, default=false): Display per sub-solver search statistics when log_search_progress is enabled.\n\n## Other Debugging Parameters\n- **debug_postsolve_with_full_solver** (bool, default=false): Use full solver for postsolve instead of default approach.\n\n**Note:** The parameters `log_callback`, `dump_problem_proto`, `linearization_level`, and `share_level_zero_bounds` appear in the provided excerpt, though detailed descriptions for some are limited in the visible portion."}]},"uuid":"387e4bc0-1910-4dc5-9b79-6fbead3780fa","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:45.046Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c6b3afbf-18af-456d-a398-0be4f4737fdf","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"7578d1c9-8da7-4096-afb9-fda8d4a7c8e0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"58edd382-d924-48ac-8751-7dee8400aa54","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E6r8A3ybZLYBJTcxCqYof4","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Log Parser Blocks\n\nBased on the GitHub page, the repository contains block parsers in the `src/cpsat_logutils/blocks/` directory. The documentation references these specific block classes:\n\n1. **SolverBlock** – Extracts solver metadata like version, worker count, and parameters\n2. **InitialModelBlock** – Parses initial variable and constraint counts\n3. **PresolvedModelBlock** – Captures presolved model dimensions\n4. **PresolveSummaryBlock** – Determines if presolve solved the problem\n5. **SearchProgressBlock** – Retrieves presolve timing and search events\n6. **TaskTimingBlock** – Extracts task timing information (exportable to pandas)\n7. **SearchStatsBlock** – Parses search statistics data\n8. **ObjectiveBoundsBlock** – Extracts objective bound information\n9. **ResponseBlock** – Captures final solver status and objective value\n\nThe documentation states: \"explore its block-specific methods in the blocks/ directory\" but doesn't provide an exhaustive list of all block classes or their specific regex patterns. The page focuses on demonstrating usage patterns rather than documenting the complete internal parsing architecture.\n\nFor the full inventory of blocks and parsing logic, you'd need to examine the actual source code in the repository's `blocks/` subdirectory."}]},"uuid":"6c68c683-4d91-489f-aaee-4ed2baaa0985","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:47.824Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7578d1c9-8da7-4096-afb9-fda8d4a7c8e0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"c8d6a700-364d-4f5d-bb08-150dd4a254bc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"58edd382-d924-48ac-8751-7dee8400aa54","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MWpWTCdqtq2WPvXxqGeUyv","type":"tool_result","content":"# Public APIs for Learned Clauses and Solver Internals\n\n## Key Methods for Conflict/Clause Export\n\n**ConflictCallback typedef:**\n```cpp\ntypedef absl::FunctionRef<void(ClausePtr, absl::Span<const Literal>)>\n    ConflictCallback;\n```\nInvoked when new conflict clauses are learned during search.\n\n**Clause extraction:**\n```cpp\ntemplate <typename Output>\nbool ExtractClauses(Output* out)\n```\nExports problem clauses via `AddBinaryClause()` and `AddClause()` callbacks on the output object.\n\n## Trail and Decision Access\n\n```cpp\nconst Trail& LiteralTrail() const\nconst VariablesAssignment& Assignment() const\nconst std::vector<LiteralWithTrailIndex>& Decisions() const\nint CurrentDecisionLevel() const\n```\n\n## ClauseManager Access\n\n```cpp\nClauseManager* clauses_propagator_\n```\nProvides internal clause database access. Methods include:\n- `AllClausesInCreationOrder()`\n- `DeleteRemovedClauses()`\n- `IsRemovable(clause)`\n\n## Binary Clause Management\n\n```cpp\nvoid TrackBinaryClauses(bool value)\nbool AddBinaryClauses(absl::Span<const BinaryClause> clauses)\nconst std::vector<BinaryClause>& NewlyAddedBinaryClauses()\n```\n\n## LRAT Proof Support\n\nThe solver integrates with `LratProofHandler` for proof generation during conflict analysis and minimization."}]},"uuid":"44dc3eb0-69fe-49ca-8109-6b42caf0503b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:48.780Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c8d6a700-364d-4f5d-bb08-150dd4a254bc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"243c76bc-3854-4c27-a2ce-fb731539d7dc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"58edd382-d924-48ac-8751-7dee8400aa54","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TTyM53x8QJKo99geL2ucMH","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"or-tools\" \"share_binary_clauses\" \"share_glue_clauses\" worker clause sharing\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/clause.h at master · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/master/ortools/sat/clause.h\"},{\"title\":\"clause | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/sat/clause\"},{\"title\":\"Define Sharing Settings for Clause Sets and Clauses\",\"url\":\"https://help.salesforce.com/s/articleView?id=ind.sf_contracts_define_sharing_settings_for_clause_sets_and_clauses.htm&language=en_US&type=5\"},{\"title\":\"Community and LBD-Based Clause Sharing Policy for Parallel SAT Solving - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7326468/\"},{\"title\":\"Work Sharing Sample Clauses | Law Insider\",\"url\":\"https://www.lawinsider.com/clause/work-sharing\"},{\"title\":\"Job Share Sample Clauses: 845 Samples | Law Insider\",\"url\":\"https://www.lawinsider.com/clause/job-share\"},{\"title\":\"OR-Tools Release Notes | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/support/release_notes\"},{\"title\":\"Community and LBD-Based Clause Sharing Policy for Parallel SAT Solving | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-51825-7_2\"},{\"title\":\"Sharing Sample Clauses: 589 Samples | Law Insider\",\"url\":\"https://www.lawinsider.com/clause/sharing\"},{\"title\":\"Group sharing of occupation Sample Clauses | Law Insider\",\"url\":\"https://www.lawinsider.com/clause/group-sharing-of-occupation\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about OR-Tools clause handling, though the specific parameters `share_binary_clauses` and `share_glue_clauses` are not explicitly mentioned in these results.\n\nWhat I found:\n\nOR-Tools includes `BinaryClauseManager` which handles binary clauses, `BinaryImplicationGraph` which manages relationships within binary clauses, `LiteralWatchers` which tracks literal occurrences, and `SatClause` which represents a general satisfiability clause.\n\nRegarding clause sharing in parallel SAT solving more broadly: Modern parallel SAT solvers rely heavily on effective clause sharing policies for their performance, where high-quality learnt clauses are shared between the worker nodes of parallel solvers to lead to better performance. Some of the more well-known metrics to identify high-quality clauses for sharing include clause length, literal block distance (LBD), and clause usage in propagation.\n\nHowever, the search results don't contain specific documentation about the `share_binary_clauses` and `share_glue_clauses` parameters themselves. These appear to be specific configuration options in OR-Tools' SAT solver that control whether binary clauses and glue clauses (clauses with low literal block distance) are shared between worker threads during parallel solving. For detailed information about these specific parameters, you may want to check the OR-Tools GitHub repository directly or the official SAT solver configuration documentation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5de4c181-e12c-4bf9-bd57-db08f876b306","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:42:49.873Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"243c76bc-3854-4c27-a2ce-fb731539d7dc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
