{"parentUuid":"c5dee408-b654-41a7-83d4-95d6bb45c1f6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"49832040-465b-48c3-8853-fc9aaaff2d1f","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01332fkpUhWG1tQDiaLxhAeu","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Structured Data and Callbacks\n\nBased on this discussion thread, there is **no built-in structured data format or proto** for CP-SAT log search progress events.\n\nThe thread reveals:\n\n1. **Search progress is string-based**: Kevin initially asked if search progress could be \"fetched as an object\" rather than as strings, but this capability doesn't appear to exist for CP-SAT.\n\n2. **Recommended approach**: Laurent Perron, an OR-Tools developer, suggested using \"the solution callback mechanism\" for CP-SAT rather than trying to parse log output. He noted that the original CP solver uses SearchMonitor subclassing, but CP-SAT has a different callback approach.\n\n3. **No direct structured access**: The thread doesn't mention any protobuf messages or structured events for monitoring solver progress—only callbacks for solution events.\n\nKevin reportedly resolved their issue using the suggested callback approach, but the final implementation details weren't shared in the thread, leaving the exact callback mechanism undocumented here."}]},"uuid":"ca57e461-e558-4289-b9c8-11b65710f79e","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:43:14.402Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c5dee408-b654-41a7-83d4-95d6bb45c1f6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
