{"parentUuid":"bde73243-92fc-443f-a35b-cbb04cb7b873","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"49832040-465b-48c3-8853-fc9aaaff2d1f","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EqunTPbzUqDJWYMYm9WRm5","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CP-SAT log \"fj_long\" \"no_lp\" \"pseudo_costs\" subsolver names worker\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Custom combination of subsolvers\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/pQ4B7QD6ebw\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-logutils: Utils for parsing the logs of OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-logutils\"},{\"title\":\"cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.md at main · d-krupke/cpsat-primer\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer/blob/main/understanding_the_log.md\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver couldn't prove the solution is optimal if num_workers < 5 but otherwise it did instantly. · Issue #3662 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662\"},{\"title\":\"cpsat-logutils · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/cpsat-logutils/\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about CP-SAT logs and the subsolver names you mentioned. Here's what I found:\n\n## CP-SAT Subsolvers and Log Information\n\nCP-SAT uses full problem subsolvers including: core, default_lp, lb_tree_search, max_lp, no_lp, objective_lb_search, probing, pseudo_costs, quick_restart, quick_restart_no_lp, and reduced_costs. It also uses first solution subsolvers including fj_long_default, fj_short_default, fs_random, and fs_random_quick_restart.\n\nThe \"no_lp\" subsolver is the same as default_lp but without linearization. The \"pseudo_costs\" subsolver uses pseudo costs for branching, which are computed from historical changes in objective bounds following certain branching decisions.\n\nRegarding workers and parallelization: CP-SAT starts search with multiple workers (in the example shown, 16 workers). Default_lp, fixed, pseudo_costs, no_lp, max_lp, and core are complete solvers, while the rest of the workers will cycle across the remaining LNS (Large Neighborhood Search) and feasibility pump solvers.\n\nThe log output shows clauses shared by each subsolver, providing a summary of how different solution strategies contributed to the solver's performance.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"625caa87-2792-405a-a471-892bc1090810","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:43:19.474Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bde73243-92fc-443f-a35b-cbb04cb7b873","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
