{"parentUuid":"184dce7e-0e9a-4527-924a-6e1e24d74829","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_017nN8K2LGxWyBsVsYHfnTZU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PAoqy3MA44e6r44KBU7mnx","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"OR-Tools CP-SAT export to DIMACS CNF run with external SAT solver MiniSAT Glucose"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4023,"cache_read_input_tokens":43023,"output_tokens":431,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4023},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":431,"cache_read_input_tokens":43023,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4023,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4023,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaornpAKRShB35FayWsr8","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"89c87648-4c7c-4511-b582-41b4afd57ff2","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:43:26.386Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"22530b9a-dd56-491e-9aad-b0f61fccfbbc","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"49832040-465b-48c3-8853-fc9aaaff2d1f","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012wXiJKKxGkGWuTxwJzcs8G","type":"tool_result","content":"# CP-SAT Log Parser Elements\n\nBased on the provided documentation, here are the regex-parseable sections you're looking for:\n\n## Clauses Shared Section\n\nThe document shows this exact format:\n\n```\nClauses shared            Num\n                 'core':  137\n           'default_lp':    1\n       'lb_tree_search':    4\n```\n\n**Regex pattern:**\n```regex\nClauses shared\\s+Num\\n((?:\\s+'[^']+'\\s*:\\s+\\d+\\n)+)\n```\n\nIndividual entries:\n```regex\n\\s+'([^']+)'\\s*:\\s+(\\d+)\n```\n\n## Important Limitation\n\nThe provided webpage content does **not include** the specific sections you're requesting:\n- Learned clause statistics\n- LBD (Literal Block Distance) metrics\n- Conflict counts per worker\n- Restart information details\n- Search statistics tables\n\nThe document shows the \"Clauses shared\" subsection under \"Subsolver Details\" but explicitly states: *\"This is a very detailed part of the log and can be overwhelming\"* and notes it's *\"primarily intended for the developers of CP-SAT.\"*\n\n**Recommendation:** Access the actual CP-SAT solver logs directly or consult the [Log Analyzer tool](https://cpsat-log-analyzer.streamlit.app/) mentioned in the documentation, which appears to parse these metrics automatically."}]},"uuid":"963576cf-4815-49b5-b331-af7c59fc371b","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:43:29.294Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"22530b9a-dd56-491e-9aad-b0f61fccfbbc","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"59cde828-423c-4697-bb39-efe43ac1f50e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"49832040-465b-48c3-8853-fc9aaaff2d1f","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Um9WCVEdNF5FLiwr7ZLjwS","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"or-tools\" \"CpSolverResponse\" \"solution_info\" worker which subsolver string\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: Google.OrTools.Sat.CpSolverResponse Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/dotnet/classGoogle_1_1OrTools_1_1Sat_1_1CpSolverResponse.html\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.py at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.py\"},{\"title\":\"trying to solve huge mode on CP-Sat\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/VjiSYjFFB_4\"},{\"title\":\"Setting solver limits | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_tasks\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/cp_model_solver.h at master · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/master/ortools/sat/cp_model_solver.h\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/cp_model_solver.h at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/cp_model_solver.h\"},{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/docs/README.md at stable · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/docs/README.md\"},{\"title\":\"Google OR-Tools: com.google.ortools.sat.CpSolver Class Reference\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/java/classcom_1_1google_1_1ortools_1_1sat_1_1CpSolver.html\"},{\"title\":\"Original CP Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/routing/original_cp_solver\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information about `CpSolverResponse` and `solution_info` in OR-Tools:\n\nThe \"solution_info\" field in `CpSolverResponse` provides additional information about how the solution was found, and it also stores model or parameters errors that caused the model to be invalid.\n\nThe Python API includes a `solution_info()` method that returns information on the solve process.\n\nIn the Java API, `solution_info()` returns information on how the solution was found, or the reason why the model or the parameters are invalid.\n\nRegarding the \"worker\" and \"subsolver\" references in your query: In multithread mode, the statistics in `solution_info` correspond to the first subsolver, which is usually the one with the user-defined parameters or the default-search if none are specified.\n\nThe solver can use multiple workers with different subsolvers such as \"default_lp\", \"less_encoding\", \"no_lp\", \"max_lp\", \"quick_restart\", \"feasibility_pump\", \"rins_lns_default\", and \"rens_lns_default\".\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"891453a6-3e85-413e-abc6-9a3dfb206d10","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:43:30.594Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"59cde828-423c-4697-bb39-efe43ac1f50e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"184dce7e-0e9a-4527-924a-6e1e24d74829","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"49832040-465b-48c3-8853-fc9aaaff2d1f","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01V3ujfbVeKEufMSXF68xX4r","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CPMpy unsat core CP-SAT assumption Benders cut implementation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Solving with assumptions — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/unsat_core_extraction.html\"},{\"title\":\"UnSAT core extraction with assumptions — CPMpy 0.9.23 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/linearize-power/unsat_core_extraction.html\"},{\"title\":\"UnSAT core extraction with assumption variables — CPMpy 0.9.21 ...\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/unsat_core_extraction.html\"},{\"title\":\"UnSAT core extraction with assumptions — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/complex_sudoku_examples/unsat_core_extraction.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy ortools interface (cpmpy.solvers.ortools) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/stable/api/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy pysat interface (cpmpy.solvers.pysat) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/api/solvers/pysat.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy pysat interface (cpmpy.solvers.pysat) — CPMpy 0.9.23 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/min_max_bug/api/solvers/pysat.html\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy.solvers.pysat — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/_modules/cpmpy/solvers/pysat.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy z3 interface (cpmpy.solvers.z3) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/docs_solvers/api/solvers/z3.html\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy.solvers.ortools — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/cp_optimizer/_modules/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found comprehensive information about CPMpy's implementation of unsat core extraction with assumptions and CP-SAT.\n\n## Summary of Search Results\n\nLazy Clause Generation solvers like OR-Tools are built on SAT solvers and hence can inherit the ability to define assumptions and extract an unsatisfiable core. Since version 8.2, OR-Tools supports declaring assumptions and extracting an unsat core.\n\nCPMpy implements this functionality using PySAT-like `s.solve(assumptions=[...])` and `s.get_core()` methods, and this opens the door to more advanced use cases, such as Minimal Unsatisfiable Subsets (MUS) and QuickXplain-like tools to help debugging.\n\n### How It Works\n\nThe `solve()` method accepts a list of CPMpy Boolean variables (or their negation) that are assumed to be true. For repeated solving and/or for use with `get_core()`, if the model is UNSAT, `get_core()` returns a small subset of assumption variables that are unsat together.\n\nCPMpy returns only those variables that are False in the UNSAT core, though there is no guarantee that the core is minimal. However, this interface opens up the possibility to add more advanced Minimal Unsatisfiable Subset algorithms on top.\n\n### Implementation Details\n\nCPMpy implements a simple MUS deletion-based algorithm using assumptions. The implementation is available across multiple solver backends (OR-Tools CP-SAT, PySAT, and Z3), allowing users to leverage unsat core extraction with whichever solver they prefer.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"777cc68e-736e-4954-9e5d-963a3b8b5185","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:43:32.198Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"184dce7e-0e9a-4527-924a-6e1e24d74829","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"89c87648-4c7c-4511-b582-41b4afd57ff2","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"49832040-465b-48c3-8853-fc9aaaff2d1f","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PAoqy3MA44e6r44KBU7mnx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"OR-Tools CP-SAT export to DIMACS CNF run with external SAT solver MiniSAT Glucose\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - elben/sat: SAT solver assistant. Converts propositions (p ^ q) ==> CNF ==> DIMACS CNF files.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/elben/sat\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-primer: The CP-SAT Primer: Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer\"},{\"title\":\"SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://homes.cs.washington.edu/~kevinz/sat-solver/\"},{\"title\":\"Sat\",\"url\":\"https://doc.sagemath.org/html/en/reference/sat/index.html\"},{\"title\":\"PySAT Documentation Release 1.9.dev2\",\"url\":\"https://pysathq.github.io/docs/pysat.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Google AI’s OR-Tools CP-SAT Solver unofficial tutorial Bobak Pezeshki\",\"url\":\"https://ics.uci.edu/~dechter/courses/ics-275/fall-2020/slides/OR-Tools_CP-SAT_Solver_Tutorial.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"SAT solver - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SAT_solver\"},{\"title\":\"SAT-Solvers via DIMACS Files - Sat\",\"url\":\"https://doc.sagemath.org/html/en/reference/sat/sage/sat/solvers/dimacs.html\"},{\"title\":\"ortools.sat.python.cp_model API documentation\",\"url\":\"https://or-tools.github.io/docs/pdoc/ortools/sat/python/cp_model.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about OR-Tools CP-SAT and DIMACS CNF format with external SAT solvers. Here's what I found:\n\nThe CP-SAT solver is designed for integer programming problems and is generally faster than MPSolver. However, the search results indicate that while OR-Tools provides CP-SAT functionality, there doesn't appear to be direct documentation about exporting CP-SAT models to DIMACS CNF format in the official OR-Tools documentation.\n\nRegarding external SAT solvers like MiniSAT and Glucose, the search results show that these are indeed compatible with DIMACS CNF format. Examples of solvers include clasp and MiniSat, and the DIMACS CNF format is the standard for interfacing with external SAT solvers. Additionally, Sage ships with pre-written interfaces for RSat and Glucose.\n\nThe search results show that Google's CP-SAT solver, part of OR-Tools, won gold medals at the Minizinc constraint programming competitions in editions 2018 up until 2025, indicating it's a powerful solver. However, the available documentation doesn't explicitly describe a built-in feature for exporting CP-SAT models directly to DIMACS CNF format to run with external solvers like MiniSAT or Glucose.\n\nIf you're looking to do this specific workflow, you may need to check the OR-Tools GitHub repository or community forums for any community-contributed solutions or tools that enable this conversion.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c27755ee-590a-44e4-99e1-e5d92ab79526","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:43:32.520Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"89c87648-4c7c-4511-b582-41b4afd57ff2","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
