{"parentUuid":"47919b3b-d9f7-4725-aaaa-54bdef79cae8","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JcoFhqGqUh1ozK49StEUaJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KmymkxcYfAgQqXQqTp4MmL","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"or-tools\" CP-SAT \"Search stats\" per worker \"conflicts\" \"restarts\" \"branches\" \"Clauses\" log line format"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4735,"cache_read_input_tokens":47046,"output_tokens":223,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4735},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":223,"cache_read_input_tokens":47046,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4735,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4735,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoroxYd8FTHXqBKbUvCi","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"dfcabafb-2a86-4594-9595-6b31cb58a2da","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:43:39.983Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"dfcabafb-2a86-4594-9595-6b31cb58a2da","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b51b1f8-77f0-4694-9f17-7a38a67bdbcd","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KmymkxcYfAgQqXQqTp4MmL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"or-tools\" CP-SAT \"Search stats\" per worker \"conflicts\" \"restarts\" \"branches\" \"Clauses\" log line format\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT claims to find optimal solution to a MILP\",\"url\":\"https://groups.google.com/g/or-tools-discuss/c/4fcAuWiIUFA\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT Solver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/cp/cp_solver\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver takes way too long to shut down or does not stop at all despite given time limit · Issue #4882 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/4882\"},{\"title\":\"SatSolver | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/sat/sat_solver/SatSolver\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT get's stuck when trying to maximize sum of boolean variables that are all added as assumptions · google/or-tools · Discussion #3630\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3630\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding CP-SAT: Constraint Programming Meets SAT Solving | by Jonas Poelmans | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@jonaspoelmans120/understanding-cp-sat-constraint-programming-meets-sat-solving-b137dddb943c\"},{\"title\":\"CP-SAT solver couldn't prove the solution is optimal if num_workers < 5 but otherwise it did instantly. · Issue #3662 · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/3662\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"Parameters - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about OR-Tools CP-SAT solver log format and the statistics it tracks, particularly regarding the per-worker search statistics.\n\nCP-SAT logs include search statistics such as conflicts, branches, propagations, integer propagations, restarts, and lp_iterations. These appear in the CpSolverResponse summary section of the logs.\n\nDuring the search phase, CP-SAT logs progress for each worker with information including timing, best solution found, and next bound estimates. The solver tracks statistics including branches, failures, propagations, and restarts.\n\nAdditionally, CP-SAT logs information about shared clauses across different solver strategies, showing counts for various solver types like 'core', 'default_lp', 'lb_tree_search', 'max_lp', 'no_lp', 'objective_lb_search', 'pseudo_costs', 'quick_restart', 'quick_restart_no_lp', and 'reduced_costs'.\n\nThe search results show that the log format captures these metrics both during the solving process and in the final summary section, though the specific per-worker \"Search stats\" line format you're asking about wasn't explicitly detailed in the available search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"86f64b0a-88d1-474f-a377-d26d20417a66","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:43:46.265Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dfcabafb-2a86-4594-9595-6b31cb58a2da","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"47919b3b-d9f7-4725-aaaa-54bdef79cae8","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"6b51b1f8-77f0-4694-9f17-7a38a67bdbcd","agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DgBxaJNtGwdrirsHrvCN3e","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"cpsat-log-analyzer streamlit search stats per worker conflicts restarts\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cpsat-logutils · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/cpsat-logutils/\"},{\"title\":\"Streamlit\",\"url\":\"https://cpsat-log-analyzer.streamlit.app/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/cpsat-logutils: Utils for parsing the logs of OR-Tools' CP-SAT solver.\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-logutils\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - d-krupke/CP-SAT-Log-Analyzer: A webapp that visualizes and annotates your ortools' CP-SAT logs. Partially inspired by gurobi-logtools. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/CP-SAT-Log-Analyzer\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding the Log - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html\"},{\"title\":\"cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.md at main · d-krupke/cpsat-primer\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-primer/blob/main/understanding_the_log.md\"},{\"title\":\"Collecting usage statistics failure - Community Cloud - Streamlit\",\"url\":\"https://discuss.streamlit.io/t/collecting-usage-statistics-failure/53327\"},{\"title\":\"Disable user stats for app deployed in Streamlit community cloud - Community Cloud - Streamlit\",\"url\":\"https://discuss.streamlit.io/t/disable-user-stats-for-app-deployed-in-streamlit-community-cloud/72512\"},{\"title\":\"Should not default to collecting usage statistics · Issue #7202 · streamlit/streamlit\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/streamlit/streamlit/issues/7202\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - dadicharan/Log-Analyzer: Log Analyzer with AI is a Streamlit-based tool for AI-powered log analysis. It supports CSV log uploads, data visualization (Plotly & Matplotlib), and anomaly detection using DeepSeek LLM via Ollama API. Users can explore logs, detect patterns, and gain AI-driven insights. 🚀 Python, Pandas, Streamlit, AI\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/dadicharan/Log-Analyzer\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about the CP-SAT Log Analyzer:\n\nThe CP-SAT Log Analyzer is a Streamlit app to explore logs interactively, and it's a webapp that visualizes and annotates ortools' CP-SAT logs, partially inspired by gurobi-logtools.\n\nThe related library extracts key information from CP-SAT logs (solutions, bounds, presolve stats, subsolver activity, search progress, conflicts, etc.), and exposes them in structured Python objects you can analyze or visualize.\n\nThe search results indicate that the system can track various metrics including:\n- Conflicts, branches, propagations, integer propagations, and restarts from the solver's response summary\n- Search statistics and worker-related information\n\nThe Streamlit app has an entry point at app.py with implementation in _app, and includes a parser and log documentation in cpsat_log_parser. You can access the live app at https://cpsat-log-analyzer.streamlit.app/ to explore and visualize CP-SAT logs with statistics like per-worker search data, conflicts, and restarts.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"be7a16ca-e1ad-4e71-ad34-90024ac9d7e6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:43:49.046Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"47919b3b-d9f7-4725-aaaa-54bdef79cae8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"be7a16ca-e1ad-4e71-ad34-90024ac9d7e6","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"aeef0d5e64a3cfeb9","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0196QngKrhGkr11PiPdoZGuh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough comprehensive material to write the report.\n\n# 调研报告：从 CP-SAT log 反向提取 conflict / clause 信息\n\n## 1. CP-SAT log 完整字段说明\n\n`log_search_progress=True` 的 log 由块（block）组成，每个块结构稳定。`solver.log_callback = fn` 把每行 log 喂给回调（避免重复输出）。已知块类型：`SolverBlock`（版本/参数/worker 数）、`InitialModelBlock`（变量/约束类型计数：`#kBoolOr`、`#kLinear1` 等）、`PresolvedModelBlock`、`PresolveSummaryBlock`、`SearchProgressBlock`（事件行 `EVENT | TIME | BEST | RANGE | COMMENT`，事件名 `#1/#2/#Bound/#Model`）、`TaskTimingBlock`（subsolver 用时）、`SearchStatsBlock`、`ObjectiveBoundsBlock`、`ResponseBlock`（最终统计）。Subsolver 名固定枚举：`core / default_lp / no_lp / max_lp / lb_tree_search / objective_lb_search / probing / pseudo_costs / quick_restart / quick_restart_no_lp / reduced_costs / fj_long_default / fj_short_default / fs_random / fs_random_quick_restart` 等。([CP-SAT Primer log 解析](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html), [cpsat-logutils](https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-logutils))\n\n## 2. 从 log 能反向工程的信息\n\n可拿到的：每个 subsolver 的 conflict 数、branches、propagations、restarts；`Clauses shared` 段（如 `'core': 137`）能看出哪个 worker 学到的 binary/glue clauses 最多，间接反映哪个搜索方向贡献大；事件行能定位 bound 跳变的时间和发起 worker。**拿不到**：具体哪些变量在 conflict 里、partial assignment、unsat core、learned clause 的字面量本身——这些 log 里没有。Laurent Perron 在 issue #973 / discussion #3873 的回复一贯是\"用 assumptions + sufficient_assumptions_for_infeasibility\"，明确不暴露 learned clauses。\n\n## 3. DRAT / LRAT 证明日志\n\n`sat_parameters.proto` 里有 `output_drat_proof`、`check_drat_proof`、`output_lrat_proof`、`check_lrat_proof`、`check_merged_lrat_proof`、`debug_crash_if_lrat_check_fails`。**关键限制（截至 2025-11）**：DRAT/LRAT 输出只对 pure SAT、单 worker、`presolve=NO_PRESOLVE`、`linearization_level<=1` 有效（`SatSolver::problem_is_pure_sat_` 字段把关）。我们的 master 是带 linear/integer 的 CP，输不出 DRAT。LRAT 的检查是内部一致性校验，不暴露给用户。证明文件本身（如果能输出）是 GB 级，DRAT-trim 检查比解题还慢。([DRAT writer 头文件](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/drat_checker.h), [sat_parameters.proto](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto))\n\n## 4. CpSolverResponse 完整 stats 字段\n\nC++/Python proto 字段：`status`、`objective_value`、`best_objective_bound`、`num_booleans`、`num_fixed_booleans`、`num_integers`、`num_conflicts`、`num_branches`、`num_binary_propagations`、`num_integer_propagations`、`num_restarts`、`num_lp_iterations`、`wall_time`、`user_time`、`deterministic_time`、`gap_integral`、`solution_fingerprint`、`solution_info`（字符串，写明哪个 subsolver 拿到当前解）、`solve_log`（如果开启）、`additional_solutions`、`tightened_variables`、`sufficient_assumptions_for_infeasibility`（**这是唯一官方导出的\"unsat core\"接口**，返回 assumption 索引列表）。([CpSolverResponse 字段](https://or-tools.github.io/docs/dotnet/classGoogle_1_1OrTools_1_1Sat_1_1CpSolverResponse.html))\n\n## 5. solution_callback 与 partial assignment\n\n`CpSolverSolutionCallback.on_solution_callback()` 只在**找到完整可行解**时触发，能拿到所有变量的 `BooleanValue()` / `Value()`，但**拿不到 partial assignment、conflict trail、决策树**。CP-SAT 没有 SearchMonitor 那种 \"on_decision/on_failure\" 钩子。对 conflict mining 价值有限，但对于\"收集所有 feasible 解作为正样本\"有用。\n\n## 6. GitHub 上的相关 issue\n\nissue [#973](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/973)（infeasible constraints 提取）、discussion [#3630](https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3630)（assumptions 卡住）、discussion [#3873](https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3873)（log 解析）。Perron 一贯立场：**learned clauses 不导出，用 assumptions API 拿 unsat core**。社区方案是 cpsat-logutils + CP-SAT-Log-Analyzer streamlit 应用，止步于宏观统计。\n\n## 7. MUS 提取\n\nPySAT 的 `pysat.examples.musx`（deletion-based）、`pysat.examples.optux`（最小 MUS via 隐式 hitting set）、QuickXplain（按 soft 序求偏好 MUS）。CPMpy 的 `s.solve(assumptions=...)` + `s.get_core()` 在 CP-SAT 后端上把 `sufficient_assumptions_for_infeasibility` 包成简洁 API，再叠 deletion 算法做最小化。**这才是 CP 世界里\"工程化的 conflict mining\"主流路线**，不是解析 log。\n\n## 8. 第三方 SAT solver\n\nCP-SAT 没有 export-to-DIMACS 的官方功能（pure SAT 时通过 `output_drat_proof` 顺带能拿到内部子句，但限制太死）。把整个 master 转 SAT 用 MiniSAT/Glucose 跑不可行——我们有 integer 和 linear 约束。\n\n## 9. 实际可行的 mining 流水线（推荐）\n\n**不走 log parsing 路线**——log 只能拿到统计，拿不到 conflict 字面量。**走 assumption + MUS 路线**：\n\n```\nmaster_sub_failure 时：\n  1. 把候选放置/绑定决策包成 BoolVar a_i\n  2. constraint.OnlyEnforceIf(a_i)\n  3. model.AddAssumptions([a_i...])\n  4. solver.Solve()  # 单线程、无 objective\n  5. core = solver.SufficientAssumptionsForInfeasibility()\n  6. 在 core 上跑 deletion-based 最小化 (CPMpy 风格)\n  7. 把 minimal core 写成 nogood: model.AddBoolOr([a_i.Not() for a_i in core])\n  8. 持久化到 campaign state (作为 hint, 不当 proof source)\n```\n\n**性能**：单次 MUS 提取 = O(|core|) 次 solve；可以异步、不阻塞主搜索。**工程量**：~600 行，集中在 `src/search/conflict_mining/`。\n\n## 10. CpModelProto / ResponseProto\n\n`CpModelProto` 字段：`variables[]`、`constraints[]`（`ConstraintProto` 含 `linear/bool_or/bool_and/...` 各种 oneof）、`objective`、`assumptions[]`（这里塞 var index）。`CpSolverResponse` proto 见第 4 点。`solution_info` 字符串通常形如 `\"default_lp (fixed_search)\"`，能 regex 抽出 subsolver 名。\n\n---\n\n## 实施 C 方案 mining 部分的具体技术路线\n\n**结论：放弃 log parsing 作为 conflict mining 主路径，采用 assumption + MUS。**\n\n| 方面 | 推荐 | 备选 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 数据源 | `solver.sufficient_assumptions_for_infeasibility()` | `solver.solve_log` regex（仅辅助，提 subsolver 贡献度） |\n| API | `model.add_assumptions([lit...])` + `OnlyEnforceIf` | cpsat-logutils 的 `SearchProgressBlock / TaskTimingBlock` 拿宏观统计喂 AI |\n| 最小化 | CPMpy `tools.explain.mus` 或自写 deletion 循环 | PySAT QuickXplain（要先 CNF 化，不划算） |\n| 输出 | `BoolOr([a.Not() for a in core])` 作为 hint clause 写 campaign state | 不写 checkpoint/proof（AI 安全合约） |\n| 性能 | 单次 ~|core| 次小型 solve，开 `num_search_workers=1`、关 objective | 异步 worker，与主搜索解耦 |\n| 限制 | 当前模式不能与 objective 共存——需要拆出\"可行性子问题\" | LRAT/DRAT 路线**不可用**（pure SAT only） |\n| 工程量 | ~600 行 + 1 个新模块 `src/search/conflict_mining/` | 解析 log 拿 `Clauses shared` 表喂 AI 排序，~150 行 |\n\n**两条线并行最优**：MUS 提供 nogood（精确、可重用），log 解析提供 subsolver 贡献度统计（用于 AI 候选排序的 feature）。两者都遵守 AI safety contract——nogood 当 hint，不当 proof。\n\n## Sources\n\n- [CP-SAT Primer: Understanding the Log](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/understanding_the_log.html)\n- [cpsat-logutils on GitHub](https://github.com/d-krupke/cpsat-logutils)\n- [cpsat-logutils on PyPI](https://pypi.org/project/cpsat-logutils/)\n- [CP-SAT Log Analyzer (Streamlit)](https://cpsat-log-analyzer.streamlit.app/)\n- [CP-SAT Primer: Parameters](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/05_parameters.html)\n- [CpSolverResponse class reference](https://or-tools.github.io/docs/dotnet/classGoogle_1_1OrTools_1_1Sat_1_1CpSolverResponse.html)\n- [sat_parameters.proto on GitHub](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/sat_parameters.proto)\n- [sat_solver.h on GitHub](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/master/ortools/sat/sat_solver.h)\n- [drat_checker.h on GitHub](https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/stable/ortools/sat/drat_checker.h)\n- [or-tools issue #973: best way to find infeasible constraints](https://github.com/google/or-tools/issues/973)\n- [or-tools discussion #3873: enable the log of CP-SAT](https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3873)\n- [or-tools discussion #3630: CP-SAT stuck with assumption maximization](https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3630)\n- [CPMpy: UnSAT core extraction with assumptions](https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/unsat_core_extraction.html)\n- [PySAT musx: deletion-based MUS extractor](https://pysathq.github.io/docs/html/api/examples/musx.html)\n- [PySAT OptUx: SMUS enumerator](https://pysathq.github.io/docs/html/api/examples/optux.html)\n- [Hooker: Logic-Based Benders Decomposition](https://johnhooker.tepper.cmu.edu/encyLBBD.pdf)\n- [Fast and Verified UNSAT Certificate Checking (IJCAR 2024)](https://www21.in.tum.de/~lammich/isabelle_llvm_par/IJCAR2024.pdf)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1274,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1522,"cache_read_input_tokens":51781,"output_tokens":4372,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1522},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1274,"output_tokens":4372,"cache_read_input_tokens":51781,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1522,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1522,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaorpzcAtsos7Y6eXXkLK","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"620f6d50-482f-4de9-90f5-f68fd1d27ea0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T20:45:01.970Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
